  "Discord members": "Discord 成員",
  "Monitoring": "監測",
  "Platforms": "平台",
  "Origin": "起源",
  "In 2018 I was watching an earthquake livestream and asked another person in the chat, someone who was also recording earthquakes, whether we could keep talking on Discord. That question became TWERG.": "2018 年，我在看地震直播時，問了聊天室裡另一位同樣在記錄地震的人，能不能到 Discord 繼續聊。昔日問題，後來變成了 TWERG。",
  "It grew into the earliest long-running earth science community on Discord in the Chinese-speaking world: earthquakes, typhoons, heavy rain and everything in between, shared as fast and as accurately as we can.": "它成長為中文圈最早、以 Discord 為主的長期地球科學社群：地震、颱風、豪雨，以及其間的一切，我們都盡可能又快又準地分享出去。",
  "Timeline": "時間軸",
  "TWERG is founded": "TWERG 成立",
  "A Discord server for people who record earthquakes.": "一個給記錄地震的人的 Discord 伺服器。",
  "Beyond Taiwan": "走進國際",
  "Japan Meteorological Agency data joins the feed; the first community seismology exam is held.": "接入日本氣象廳資料；舉辦第一次社群地震考試。",
  "A full earth science platform": "完整的地球科學平台",
  "Earthquakes are joined by weather, typhoons and the rest of earth science; the entry exam is retired so anyone can join.": "除了地震，也加入天氣、颱風與其他地球科學；取消入群考試，讓任何人都能加入。",
  "Website v3 and DYFI": "網站 v3 與 DYFI",
  "A rebuilt twerg.org launches with a scientific felt-report system.": "重新打造的 twerg.org 上線，並推出具科學依據的體感回報系統。",
  "The largest earth science community on Discord in the Chinese-speaking world.": "中文圈規模最大的 Discord 地球科學社群。",
  "What I built": "我做的東西",
  "Five things,": "五件作品，",
  "built by hand.": "親手打造。",
  "The twerg.org home page": "twerg.org 首頁",
  "01 / Website": "01 / 網站",
  "The community's home: live earthquake reports, a notable-earthquake archive, a changelog and policies. Built by me, in four languages.": "社群核心：即時地震報告、顯著地震資料庫、更新日誌與使用規範。由我打造，支援四種語言。",
  "A felt-intensity map of Taiwan built from public reports": "由民眾回報繪製的台灣體感震度地圖",
  "02 / DYFI": "02 / DYFI",
  "Did You Feel It?": "您感受到了嗎？",
  "A felt-report system that turns what people feel into a town-level intensity map, checked against instruments. More on it below.": "把人們的感受轉換成鄉鎮級震度地圖的體感回報系統，並與儀器資料交叉比對。下面有更多說明。",
  "A heavy rain advisory map of Taiwan": "台灣豪雨特報地圖",
  "03 / Heavy rain": "03 / 豪雨",
  "Rain advisory map": "豪雨特報地圖",
  "Official heavy rain advisories redrawn as a clean town-level map, paired with a second map for work and school closures.": "把官方的豪雨特報重新繪製成清楚的鄉鎮級地圖，並搭配另一張停班停課地圖。",
  "A typhoon warning map with forecast track and wind radii": "包含預測路徑與暴風半徑的颱風警報圖",
  "04 / Typhoon": "04 / 颱風",
  "Typhoon track map": "颱風路徑圖",
  "Forecast track, potential path, storm radii and warning areas in one frame, built to be shared as soon as a warning is issued.": "預測路徑、潛勢範圍、暴風半徑與警戒區域收進同一張圖，警報一發布就能立刻分享。",
  "05 / System": "05 / 系統",
  "Readable by everyone": "每個人都看得懂",
  "Hazard colors follow a color-universal design palette so they stay distinguishable for color-blind readers, with no decorative gradients or glow.": "災害配色採用色彩通用設計，讓色覺辨識不同的讀者也能分辨；不用裝飾性的漸層與光暈。",
  "Deep dive": "深入",
  "DYFI,": "體感回報，",
  "done properly.": "深入研究成果。",
  "A shaking map built from people instead of sensors. Getting it right meant reading the research, and then finding where a naive version goes wrong.": "一張由人而不是感測器畫出來的震度地圖。要做對，得先讀懂研究，再找出直覺做法錯在哪裡。",
  "How a felt report becomes a map": "一筆體感回報如何變成地圖",
  "Reports": "回報",
  "Consensus": "共識",
  "Intensity": "震度",
  "Check": "驗證",
  "Map": "地圖",
  "01 / Foundation": "01 / 基礎",
  "Built on USGS \"Did You Feel It?\"": "以 USGS「Did You Feel It?」為基礎",
  "The method follows the USGS framework for community decimal intensity, then maps the result onto the Central Weather Administration's own intensity scale so it speaks the same language as official reports.": "方法沿用 USGS 的社區十進位震度（CDI）框架，再把結果對應到中央氣象署的震度分級，讓它和官方報告說同一種語言。",
  "02 / The mistake I fixed": "02 / 我修正的錯誤",
  "Never average people.": "永不平均人群。",
  "The obvious approach, scoring each person and averaging the scores, quietly breaks: someone who was outdoors cannot answer the indoor questions, and a naive average drags the whole area down. Following Quitoriano and Wald, the system first finds the community's consensus on each question, then computes one intensity for the area.": "直覺的做法是替每個人算分再取平均，但它會悄悄出錯：人在戶外的人無法回答室內的題目，直接平均會把整個地區的震度拉低。依照 Quitoriano 與 Wald 的做法，系統先找出社區對每一題的共識，再為整個地區算出一個震度。",
  "03 / The questions": "03 / 問卷",
  "Three kinds of evidence": "三種證據",
  "What people felt, what moved indoors and what happened outside are weighed as separate factors, with an anchor question that grounds the rest.": "人的感受、室內物品的晃動、戶外發生的事，分成三個因子各自衡量，並有一道錨定題作為基準。",
  "04 / Place": "04 / 地點",
  "Town by town": "一個鄉鎮一個鄉鎮",
  "Reports are located to their town, grouped on a grid and cleaned of outliers. \"I didn't feel it\" is kept too, because it marks where the shaking stopped.": "回報會定位到所在的鄉鎮、以網格聚合，並過濾離群值。「我沒有感覺」也會保留，因為它標出了搖晃停止的地方。",
  "05 / Trust": "05 / 可信度",
  "Checked against instruments": "與儀器比對",
  "Every area is compared with nearby seismic stations and with an intensity prediction model, so reports that do not fit the physics are flagged.": "每個地區都會和附近的地震測站、以及震度預測模型比對，不符合物理規律的回報會被標記出來。",
  "06 / Privacy": "06 / 隱私",
  "Nothing personal kept": "不留下個人資料",
