  "Beyond": "超越",
  "the Point": "點源",
  "Estimating earthquake shaking when the rupture has a direction.": "當地震的破裂有方向時，如何估計搖晃的程度。",
  "The problem": "問題",
  "A point": "一個點，",
  "is not a fault.": "不是一條斷層。",
  "Early warning systems usually treat an earthquake as a single point, so predicted shaking fades the same way in every direction. That works for small events.": "地震預警系統通常把地震當成一個點，因此預估的搖晃會往每個方向以相同的速度衰減。對小地震來說，這樣沒問題。",
  "Large, shallow earthquakes are different. The rupture <strong>travels</strong> along the fault, and it throws stronger shaking ahead of itself. Places in that direction can feel far more than a point-source estimate says. In early warning, that is the worst kind of error: <strong>telling people it is weaker than it is.</strong>": "大型的淺層地震不一樣。破裂會沿著斷層<strong>移動</strong>，並把更強的搖晃推向前方。位在那個方向的地方，感受到的可能遠比點源估計大得多。在地震預警裡，這是最糟的一種錯誤：<strong>告訴大家搖得比實際還輕。</strong>",
  "The method": "方法",
  "01 / Listen": "01 / 傾聽",
  "Watch the shaking fade": "看搖晃怎麼衰減",
  "As stations report in, compare how quickly peak ground acceleration drops off toward the east, south, west and north.": "隨著測站陸續回傳資料，比較最大地動加速度（PGA）往東、南、西、北衰減的速度。",
  "02 / Infer": "02 / 推論",
  "Find the direction": "找出方向",
  "If shaking fades unevenly, the rupture is moving. The imbalance points the way it is travelling.": "如果各方向的衰減不一致，代表破裂正在移動；這個不平衡，就指向它前進的方向。",
  "03 / Correct": "03 / 修正",
  "Raise what lies ahead": "調高前方的震度",
  "Areas in front of the rupture get their estimated intensity raised. Areas behind it are left alone.": "破裂前方地區的預估震度會被調高，後方的地區則維持不變。",
  "04 / Update": "04 / 更新",
  "Keep listening": "持續傾聽",
  "The estimate is not a one-time calculation. It moves up and down every second as new data arrives, and is only pushed to people once it makes sense.": "這個估計不是一次算完就結束。它會隨著新資料每秒上下調整，等結果合理了才推送給大家。",
  "Directivity correction informed by Jan et al. (2018). Station data from the P-Alert network.": "方向性修正參考 Jan et al.（2018）。測站資料來自 P-Alert 觀測網。",
